                <head>I. Revision of United States neutrality legislation</head>
                <p>[See also the following releases:</p>
                <p>Letter of the Secretary of State to Senator Pittman and Representative Bloom, May
                    27, 1939, Department of State <hi rendition="#italic">Press Releases</hi>, June
                    3, 1939, p. 475.</p>
                <p>Statement by the Secretary of State, July 1, 1939, Department of State <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, July 1, 1939, p. 4.</p>
                <p>Message from the President to Congress, July 14, 1939, transmitting a statement
                    by the Secretary of State on peace and neutrality, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ibid.</hi>, July 15, 1939, p. 43.</p>
                <p>Statement of the Secretary of State at his press conference, July 11, 1939, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, p. 47.</p>
                <p>Statements released to the press by the White House, July 18, 1939, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, July 22, 1939, p. 57.</p>
                <p>Statement by the Secretary of State, September 21, 1939, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ibid.</hi>, September 23, 1939, p. 280.</p>
                <p>Press release regarding the White House conference on neutrality, September 20,
                    1939, <hi rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, p. 281.</p>
                <p>Statement by the Secretary of State, November 4, 1939, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ibid.</hi>, November 4, 1939, p. 453.]</p>































